# {{PROJECT_TITLE}}

**Your only filing job: drop anything new into [[03 Inbox]].** Claude dates it, renames it, files it, archives the original, and updates everything downstream.

## Where things are
- [[01 Master]] — the always-current picture. Start with [[01 Master/Master Summary|Master Summary]].
- [[01 Master/Settled — do not re-open|Settled — do not re-open]] — questions already answered. Claude checks this before "correcting" anything.
- [[02 Chronicle]] — what happened, in order: [[02 Chronicle/Timeline|Timeline]] and [[02 Chronicle/Prompt Log|Prompt Log]].
- [[04 Critiques]] — independent critiques of advice received.
- [[05 Trends]] — numbers over time.
- [[06 Reference]] — background, plus the untouched [[Raw Archive]].
- [[07 Deep Dives]] — research written on demand.

## Setting up on your computer

*{{#if shared}}Each co-user does this once, on their own machine. {{/if}}Skip if Claude is
already working in this folder.*

**1. Make the folder available offline — do this first.**
{{#if cloud_folder}}
> **{{CLOUD_PROVIDER}}:** {{PROVIDER_OFFLINE}}

This is not optional housekeeping. A file left in the cloud **reads as an empty file rather
than erroring**, so Claude sees a blank Master Summary, concludes there is nothing there, and
writes a "corrected" version over it. {{#if shared}}The setting is per-machine, so your choice
here affects what {{CO_USER_OTHER}} loses.{{/if}}
{{/if}}{{#if local_folder}}
This folder is on local disk, so there is nothing to configure. If you ever move it into
iCloud, Dropbox, Google Drive or OneDrive, come back and read this section again — and re-run
`--reconfigure --provider <name>` so the engine picks up that provider's hazards.
{{/if}}

**2. Point Claude Cowork at this folder.** Open the Claude desktop app → Cowork → **Add Folder**
→ select **this folder** (the one containing `CLAUDE.md`). Claude reads `CLAUDE.md`
automatically at the start of every chat here, so there is nothing to paste or configure.

**3. Check that reads are trustworthy** before doing any real work:

> Run preflight on this folder and tell me if anything is wrong.

It writes a canary, reads it back, and refuses if it finds cloud-placeholder or empty files.
Two seconds, and it is the only check that catches step 1 being wrong.

**4. Your first prompt.** Type:

> orient

You should get a short status of where things stand, drawn from the Master Summary, the settled
register and the open questions. **If it instead asks you to explain the history, stop** —
something is wrong with step 1 or 2, and you should not start filing on top of it.

{{#if shared}}
## You are a co-user, not a guest

You and {{CO_USER_OTHER}} have equal standing here: both file, both ask anything, both may
settle questions. Three things follow that are easy to get wrong:

- **Read [[02 Chronicle/Prompt Log|Prompt Log]] first each session.** Your Claude account cannot
  see the other person's chats. The Prompt Log is how you find out what they did — it is this
  project's shared conversation, and the reason neither of you has to be present for the other's.
- **Your Claude memory is private and will drift from theirs.** Anything that matters goes in a
  file in this folder, never in memory alone.
- **Working from a phone?** Cowork on mobile reaches this folder only while the Claude desktop
  app is open on *your* computer, and only for a session you **started on desktop**. Start it at
  your desk, resume it on the phone. Not a sync problem.

{{/if}}## Things you can type
`orient` · `log only` · `full update` · `no snapshot` · `snapshot now` · `quiet`

The full workflow lives in `CLAUDE.md`. Edit it to change how this project behaves — it is the control panel.
